plugin-qualify (0.19.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * plugin-qualify 0.19.0: the install check downloads the fc44 RPM artifact
    by the name the shared build gives it
  * plugin-qualify 0.19.0: build the RPM for fc44 only until the channel has
    a fedora 45 tree
  * plugin-qualify: .githooks/commit-msg is the shared stub of
    FreeMixer/.github v1
  * plugin-qualify 0.19.0: tools/pool-step.mjs is executable, as its shebang
    says
  * plugin-qualify 0.19.0: omx-contract floor 3.9.1, the first release with
    omx_json_write.h (the fetched 3.9.0 headers lack it, so native/ did not
    build)
  * plugin-qualify 0.19.0: drop the floor-only plugin-db BuildRequires; SPDX
    line on pin-refresh.test.ts
  * lv2: look up a URI with a scheme by URI, only a bare or file: argument is
    a path
  * clap-qualify: the pool's threads live in pool-host.c, and a run with a
    pool times nothing
  * release 0.19.0: the changelog names the helper-thread watch of the pool
    step
  * pool step: the plugin is watched on real helper threads, and a pool whose
    helpers run nothing is named
  * descriptors test: the CLAP fixture set is 23 with the four pool fixtures
  * pool step: a sweep over CLAP fixtures pins what the step said
  * pool step: the CLAP thread pool is granted by measuring it
  * pins: a uri with a space is one quoted word
  * wave-deps: plugin-db
  * The pin's repository is plugin-db: every name follows
  * native: the pin header is plugin-pin's
  * fixtures: the probe output names no machine
  * grid-runs: the live memory arm reads the runner's own answer, and CI
    cannot skip it
  * native: the JSON string literals are spelled by omx-contract's one writer
  * release: plugin-qualify 0.19.0
  * native: link pin.h consumers with pkg-config --libs plugin-hostd
  * compare-host: the script is executable, as its shebang says
  * rt-watch: the report is written through stdio, so <fcntl.h> is not
    included
  * compare: the server's log goes to a file; non-finite output fails; CLAP
    plugins by their id
  * compare: the JACK server ends on SIGTERM, and a container is told to give
    it /dev/shm
  * compare: every plugin under omx-clap-host, plugin-hostd, mod-host and jalv
  * packaging: mod-host is suggested, not recommended
  * sync: judge a distributed record again, and measure one that never took
    latency
  * packaging: the package installs its licence and the short README
  * packaging: no markdown in the packages; their descriptions name
    openmixer.org
  * docs: the notes move to openmixer.org; the comments state the behaviour
  * scan: units are spelled by omx-contract's units sheet, and no table of
    units is kept here
  * commit-msg: the shared stub with its licence lines, as
    FreeMixer/.github#119 has it
  * commit-msg: the shared stub as FreeMixer/.github#114 has it
  * ci: the shared checks run from FreeMixer/.github's public-sources-check,
    and no copy is kept here
  * fixtures: the fake.clap scan golden is omx-clap-host 0.26.4's, 24 plugins
    with abi-breaker
  * hosting codes: the generated file as main has it
  * a host with no JACK client is no evidence about the plugin; lilv is a
    hard dependency, loaded by its soname
  * tests: a host with no JACK client is no evidence, and lilv loads by its
    soname
  * sync: a memory gap alone takes the isolated step, and a plugin the step
    decided gets its pin back from its record
  * lv2-measure fixture: the abi-breaker's C symbols kept under link-time
    optimisation
  * judgment: a plugin whose call changed a callee-saved register is
    conditional, isolated only (hosting.stability.callee-saved-clobbered);
    omx-clap-core 0.26.2 floor; docs note
  * lv2-measure: every call into the plugin through omx-clap-core's guard;
    the record's abi field names the first that changed a callee-saved
    register
  * lv2-measure: abi-breaker.lv2, a fixture whose third run returns with
    callee-saved registers changed; the measurer must measure it to the end
    and name it, red

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 18:19:41 +0000
